cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these notebooks, the dataset atlas or the manifest, please cite this repository."
title: "QML x Cybersecurity: reproducible notebooks of quantum machine learning papers and a cybersecurity dataset atlas"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tehrani
    given-names: Madjid G.
    affiliation: "Edinburgh Napier University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/owlmt/QML"
url: "https://github.com/owlmt/QML"
abstract: >-
  One Google Colab notebook per published quantum-machine-learning (QML) cybersecurity paper,
  filed into 30 cybersecurity topic folders, each executed end to end with a classical baseline on
  identical inputs and a claim-by-claim comparison with the paper; plus a dataset atlas (folder
  00_Cybersecurity_Dataset_Atlas) that documents, visualises and maps to use cases every dataset the
  reproductions rely on.
keywords:
  - quantum machine learning
  - cybersecurity
  - intrusion detection
  - malware detection
  - phishing detection
  - reproducibility
  - datasets
